# Data licensing

The code in this repository is AGPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE). The data is not, and the terms differ by artifact. Read this before reusing anything under data/.

## Derived artifacts built from CC BY sources

The facility authority layer, version-drift tables, and the LGA coverage table are Produced Works derived from GRID3 NGA Health Facilities v2.0 and v3.0 and the geoBoundaries 774-LGA frame, all CC BY. So are the per-LGA tables in data/derived/ built from other attribution-only sources: WorldPop births (CC BY 4.0) and population with travel time to healthcare (WorldPop R2025A, CC BY 4.0, and the Malaria Atlas Project, CC BY). These derived artifacts are released under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). Attribution per data/ATTRIBUTION.md is required.

The per-LGA flood-exposure flags derive from NASA MODIS products, which NASA publishes as open data; NASA requests attribution, given in data/ATTRIBUTION.md.

## The ESPEN NTD summaries (non-commercial)

The per-state soil-transmitted-helminths burden summary and the per-LGA endemicity table for five diseases (and the endemicity ranks and columns built from them in the staging and mart tables) are derived from ESPEN (WHO/AFRO) data, which is published under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO. That license is NON-COMMERCIAL and share-alike. These derived summaries inherit those terms: you may copy, redistribute and adapt it for non-commercial purposes with attribution, under the same or an equivalent license. It must not be used in a commercial product without written permission from WHO/ESPEN.

## Raw inputs are not redistributed

The raw GRID3 geopackages, the raw ESPEN tables, and the WorldPop and Malaria Atlas Project rasters are not committed. Fetch them from their sources (data/sources.yml). This keeps the repository lean and avoids re-hosting a non-commercial upstream dataset.

This is an engineering reading of the published terms, not legal advice. Confirm the ESPEN terms directly before any commercial use.
